def tsv_to_markdown(text, headers, ndigits=3):
    """Tab-separated rows -> Markdown table; numeric cells are rounded, ids stay as they are."""
    def fmt(cell, is_id):
        if is_id:
            return cell
        try:
            v = float(cell)
        except ValueError:
            return cell
        return str(int(v)) if v == int(v) else f'{v:.{ndigits}f}'

    lines = ['| ' + ' | '.join(headers) + ' |', '|' + '|'.join('---' for _ in headers) + '|']
    for row in text.strip().split('\n'):
        cells = row.split('\t')
        if len(cells) != len(headers):
            raise ValueError(f'expected {len(headers)} cells, got {len(cells)}: {row[:30]!r}')
        lines.append('| ' + ' | '.join(fmt(c, i == 0) for i, c in enumerate(cells)) + ' |')
    return '\n'.join(lines)
```

Pasted tab-separated data has to be split into cells, each row checked to have the same number of cells as the header (otherwise the table will not render), and the numbers rounded for readability. The first column is an identifier, so it is left untouched: rounding or reformatting an id would change its meaning.

